{"title":"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> square blocks is arranged into a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197151a067f49bd4daa1952d1a4fac322409f0a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> square. How many different combinations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blocks can be selected from that set so that no two are in the same row or column?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb23671eac14810fed9f962a83b16ddead356b67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 100 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 125  \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 600 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 2300 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 3600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"461\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose the first square. The four remaining squares in its row and column and the square you chose exclude nine squares from being chosen next time.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> remaining blocks to be chosen for the second square. The three remaining spaces in its row and column and the square you chose must be excluded from being chosen next time.\n</p><p>Finally, the last square has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> remaining choices.\n</p><p>The number of ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460f606d78dbfff6d82628b29d30321aec667118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\cdot 16 \\cdot 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> but the order in which you chose the squares does not matter as the blocks are indistinguishable, so we divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6859713adc973d3fbe97fafef9ce829757e54b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc16a325891282648c5127af09cca9adef42b279.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{25 \\cdot 16 \\cdot 9}{3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1} = 25 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 3 = 100 \\cdot 6 = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ } 600}\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Once we choose our three squares, we will have occupied three separate columns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59db3616e539878054b9dd007abeb26d5fcde87d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A, B, C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> and three separate rows. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b200084dd6ff391d1b1d5ffeb2121e37873f6f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${5 \\choose 3} \\times {5 \\choose 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"92\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose these rows and columns. \n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to assign the square in column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to a row, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to assign the square in column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to one of the remaining two rows, and poor square in column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> doesn't get to choose. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b2d01bd4bc57aff63131d1c4ad46446d534a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$:($\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>In total, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc24d0f0e0a7dc502555585ac4f647af4acdecdb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{5 \\choose 3} \\times {5 \\choose 3} \\times 3!\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"53\" /> which totals out to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a931a508e64416937c65ba542f88aaae78865b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ } 600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"73\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~HappyHuman\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (Answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/537dfb5d845637c5322c23f6103b53ebd89ab525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{25}{3}=2300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"106\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose three blocks. However, the restriction clearly limits the number of ways we can choose our blocks. Hence, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5bdc2c0e59651ee5e6fa74ba318dc73d744feb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e226c2f5a445f0a9ab589c1337336ea7587b36e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/988a15926640244e366e55b6e468af2e3e60047e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> could be the correct answer. Clearly, there are more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> ways, thus yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fe3e0a4053786d84954515c0514e07fa3f8a0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C)} 600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" /> ways.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0W3VmFp55cM?t=4921\">https://youtu.be/0W3VmFp55cM?t=4921</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5UojVH4Cqqs?t=3460\">https://youtu.be/5UojVH4Cqqs?t=3460</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B\">2007 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a r